{"_meta":true,"allowed":75,"amounts_cents":[10,100,1000],"by_policy":{},"caveat":"Synthetic legitimate actions, NOT a production soak, and the n rows are not n independent opportunities: this is 3 configurations repeated 25 times each, so a cluster-aware reading has only 3 clusters and a correspondingly much wider bound (scoring/VERIFY.md records the 0/3 reading alongside the 0/75 one). Coverage is also narrow by construction: one provider, one operation, one sandbox, amount the only varied field — it does not exercise the gate families or any non-purchase path. The reported interval is Wilson two-sided; the one-sided rule-of-three bound is defined only at a zero numerator and is printed only there.","commit":"614d3d2","false_denials":0,"kind":"false-denials","n":75,"note":"False-denial measurement (SPEC §6). One record per legitimate action: 3 amounts × 25 repetitions = 75. Each action is set up to be correct in EVERY way — owner-approved, in scope, unexpired, correct sandbox, inside the caps — and driven through the real ToolRouter membrane, so any denial is a FALSE denial. `allowed: false` marks one; `denying_policy` is the denying policy's name (or the inspected error term, when the denial did not come from a policy). Recompute: rate = count(allowed == false) / n, and the by-policy breakdown is the frequency of `denying_policy` over those rows.","per_amount":25,"run_id":"v12-false-denials"}
